OL,3,GNEWSA'Extremely rare' Roman coins sell
OL,4,Afor #16,000
OL,5,
OL,6,FTwo Roman coins described by
OL,7,Fauctioneers as "extremely rare" have
OL,8,Ffetched #16,000 at auction after they
OL,9,Fwere unearthed in a small village.
OL,11,FThe silver denarii - the plural form of
OL,12,Fan ancient Roman silver coin - were
OL,13,Fdiscovered by a metal detectorist in
OL,14,FWestbury-on-Severn, Gloucestershire in
OL,15,FJune 2023.
OL,17,FEstimated to date back to AD 286-293,
OL,18,Fthe coins each feature a bust of
OL,19,FCarausius, an officer in the Roman
OL,20,Fmilitary service who created a
OL,21,Fshort-lived independent state in
OL,22,FBritain.
OL,23,APub: 12-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBW-SW Eng NewsC Reg TVFWeather
FL,348,340,200,160,0,100
